# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and deployed on Linux. A shell
# script with CRLF does not run there at all: bash reports a syntax error at
# the first `{` and names a line that is perfectly valid, so the reader goes
# looking at the script instead of at the bytes.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working-tree form regardless of anyone's core.autocrlf, so
# a file edited on Windows still lands on the Ubuntu box able to run.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the mirror image: these only ever run on Windows, and some
# older hosts are unhappy with LF-only scripts.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf

# Binary, so git never tries to translate anything inside them.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.exe       binary
*.zip       binary
*.gz        binary
*.tgz       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary

# The built agent binaries. No extension on Linux, so name them.
Sentora/main    binary
Sentora/main.exe binary
